{"type":"result","subtype":"success","is_error":false,"duration_ms":91304,"duration_api_ms":90789,"num_turns":22,"result":"","stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b7fed467-e57e-4cb9-8690-cadab9a9d926","total_cost_usd":0.7815179999999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":12,"cache_creation_input_tokens":59368,"cache_read_input_tokens":633916,"output_tokens":3738,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":59368,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-4-6":{"inputTokens":12,"outputTokens":3738,"cacheReadInputTokens":633916,"cacheCreationInputTokens":59368,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.7815179999999999,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":64000}},"permission_denials":[],"structured_output":{"outcome":"approved","evidence":["All 197 tests pass across tank_core, tank_data, and tank_scenarios with 0 failures.","`cargo clippy -p tank_core -p tank_data -p tank_scenarios --all-targets -- -D warnings` produces zero warnings.","`cargo fmt --all --check` produces no output — formatting is clean.","Old pH shortcut (`6.3 + log10(alk) - log10(DIC)`) is completely absent from the codebase; grep confirms no matches.","Solver is a closed-form O(1) quadratic in [H+] (chemistry.rs:270-357) using temperature-corrected pKa1 via Harned & Davis (1943). Deterministic with no iteration.","TankSnapshot (snapshot.rs:87) now reads `ph` from `carbonate_eq.ph` — the same freshly solved equilibrium used for `co2_aq_mmol_per_l` (line 120). Unit test `snapshot_uses_one_carbonate_solution_for_ph_and_co2` (snapshot.rs:202-223) locks in the self-consistency property.","`SourceWaterProfile::bicarbonate_mg_per_l` (source_water.rs:25-28) now has a doc comment: 'Display/documentation field only. Runtime carbonate chemistry uses DIC, alkalinity, and temperature as the authoritative inputs.'","Save migration v3→v4 (save.rs:324-331) is a deliberate no-op relying on serde defaults, with a comment explaining that legacy saves do not gain synthetic reserve. `migrate_v3_to_v4` does `let _ = value; Ok(())`.","Regression test `legacy_schema_v3_saves_leave_missing_reserve_at_default_zero` (save_load.rs:274-333) constructs a v3 save with 30 adults and 20 juveniles, removes `reserve_g`, migrates, and asserts `migrated.state.animal.reserve_g == 0.0`.","Shrimp feeding (shrimp.rs:140-164) now computes appetite and consumption on a consistent routing-mass basis: `food_demand_route_g` and `periph_consumed_route_g` are both converted via `algae_detrital_mass_g()`, and `detritus_demand_route_g` is derived from their difference. `daily_food_consumed_g` sums two routing-gram quantities.","Regression test `shrimp_feeding_caps_total_intake_on_routing_mass_basis` (shrimp.rs:834-877) verifies total intake equals the routing-mass daily cap and `daily_food_consumed_g` matches the sum of routing-gram components.","The old mixed-unit test `shrimp_feeding_uses_detritus_only_for_unmet_demand` is absent — replaced by the corrected routing-mass test.","All three solver fallback paths (acid_dominated, high_buffer, outside_quadratic_envelope) reproject species via `carbonate_species_for_ph()` and emit structured `tracing::debug!` diagnostics.","Source-water validation is unified: both `SourceWaterPreset::validate()` and `SourceWaterProfile::validate()` route through `validate_source_water_carbonate_profile()` (chemistry.rs:387-412) using the same solver.","Clamp-boundary documentation at chemistry.rs:337-340 explains the DIC conservation vs alkalinity consistency trade-off.","48-point parameter sweep, 5 extreme edge cases, and directional temperature response tests provide broad numerical stability coverage.","normalize_loaded_carbonate_state() (save.rs:345-354) unconditionally re-solves from canonical DIC/alkalinity/temperature on load, repairing stale caches; reconcile_stability_tracker() prevents false instability spikes."],"findings_or_gaps":["Ka2 is fixed at 10.33 without temperature correction. Documented as acceptable for freshwater pH 5.5-8.5 where CO3-- is minor, but should be revisited if extended to marine or high-pH regimes.","The `fallback_zero_dic` path does not emit a tracing diagnostic when both DIC and alkalinity are negligible (returning NEUTRAL_FALLBACK directly at chemistry.rs:212-213). Defensible since deionized-water equilibrium is not operationally interesting, but it breaks the blanket fallback diagnostic pattern.","Legacy saves with custom out-of-range source-water catalog entries still deserialize but water-change actions against those profiles now fail at runtime with InvalidSourceProfile. Correct behavior but could surprise users with old custom profiles.","The source-water carbonate validator (chemistry.rs:407) still uses strict inequality on both bounds. As identified in final-review amendment fr-4-8b7458ba, this means the fallback_zero_dic path that intentionally produces pH=8.5 would fail validation if a source-water profile triggered it. No shipped preset does, but it remains an internal contract inconsistency between the solver and the validator."],"follow_up_or_amendments":[]},"fast_mode_state":"off","uuid":"516d37c4-ca62-4f50-8386-c0fde8a0abe9"}
